6643
06:34:49,880 --> 06:35:00,080
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Kasi kung magkakaroon tayo ng project doon tapos masita ni DA, dahil ay hindi pwede yan, gagastos na yung mga investor, etc.

6644
06:35:00,420 --> 06:35:11,160
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: So mas maganda siguro na kahit inisyal, maka-identify na tayo ng mga area na pwedeng mapaglagyan para guided si DOE.

6645
06:35:11,160 --> 06:35:16,080
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Kasi yung transmission natin, ay ididikit po yan doon sa planta.

6646
06:35:16,580 --> 06:35:19,240
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Malaki po, billion-billion po yung cost ng transmission.

6647
06:35:19,880 --> 06:35:21,720
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Baka makatiwangwang kung ano.

6648
06:35:21,860 --> 06:35:27,880
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: So what I am suggesting is, these are all issues of national significance, Mr. Chair.

6649
06:35:28,360 --> 06:35:37,560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yes, Mr. Chair. Meron din kaming unwritten agreement sa ngayon with DOE na all existing projects na naumpisahan na

6650
06:35:37,560 --> 06:35:41,920
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: o kaya na bigyan na nila ng permit, itutuloy.

6651
06:35:42,560 --> 06:35:49,000
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yung mga bago lang ang hinapahold namin para maayos yung policy framework.

6652
06:35:49,000 --> 06:35:57,240
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Meron kaming nabanggit kaninang earlier this morning na i-geotag na namin yung mga reserved areas for agriculture, geofencing pala,

6653
06:35:57,680 --> 06:36:04,340
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: para malinaw na sa lahat kung anong pwede, anong hindi, kagaya ng binanggit ninyo, Mr. Chair.

6654
06:36:04,520 --> 06:36:09,620
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: And we'll hopefully finish the geofencing by end of this year, Mr. Chair.

6655
06:36:10,200 --> 06:36:12,480
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Thank you for that information, Mr. Secretary.

6656
06:36:13,440 --> 06:36:15,160
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Panghuli na lang, Mr. Secretary.

6657
06:36:15,980 --> 06:36:18,920
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Mayroon tayong bagong batas na.

6658
06:36:19,000 --> 06:36:21,240
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Mayroon tayong RA 12308.

6659
06:36:21,940 --> 06:36:33,220
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Can you brief this representation kung paano natin i-implemento yung Animal Competitiveness Fund?

6660
06:36:35,120 --> 06:36:46,900
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, basically, sa taxes na magkakolekta natin sa importasyon ng mga meats natin ng bansa, from chicken, pork, and others,

6661
06:36:47,880 --> 06:36:48,900
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: magkakaroon natin.

6662
06:36:49,000 --> 06:36:54,060
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mayroon tayong 20 billion a year ang ating livestock industry or animal industry.

6663
06:36:55,740 --> 06:37:03,360
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Majority dyan, initially, ay lalagay natin sa repopulation, about 4 to 5 billion out of the 20.

6664
06:37:03,480 --> 06:37:08,780
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So, 25% ng budget na yun will be doon ilalagay.

6665
06:37:08,920 --> 06:37:12,560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Of course, we are creating also a vaccine manufacturing facility.

6666
06:37:13,060 --> 06:37:15,540
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mayroon din tayong herd build-up.

6667
06:37:16,160 --> 06:37:17,560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mayroon din tayong mga...

6668
06:37:19,000 --> 06:37:23,200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa dairy, para taasin natin yung ating production ng dairy, among others.

6669
06:37:23,340 --> 06:37:30,220
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mayroon namang breakdown sa batas na susundin din namin, base dun sa nakalagay sa batas na sinulong natin.

6670
06:37:30,380 --> 06:37:30,900
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair.

6671
06:37:31,460 --> 06:37:31,720
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Okay.

6672
06:37:32,000 --> 06:37:37,040
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Finally, Mr. Chair, gusto ko lang paalalahanan sana.

6673
06:37:37,540 --> 06:37:44,620
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Alam ko naman, naalam ninyo ito, na hindi lang budget ang kailangan ng lahat ng government agency.

6674
06:37:45,740 --> 06:37:48,680
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Specifically, yung napakahalaga yung agriculture.

6675
06:37:48,680 --> 06:37:49,980
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Sa atin, at erikisyon.

6676
06:37:50,080 --> 06:37:54,120
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Kung hindi, mga tauhan na tapat sa servisyo.

6677
06:37:54,600 --> 06:37:58,980
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Kasi yung tatlong taon ko na halos makipag-away na ako sa plenary,

6678
06:37:59,740 --> 06:38:01,680
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: eh tao lang naman pala ang solusyon.

6679
06:38:02,520 --> 06:38:03,480
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Yung tamang tao.

6680
06:38:03,660 --> 06:38:08,260
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Kaya, kahit malaki pa yung budget ninyo,

6681
06:38:08,500 --> 06:38:14,760
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: pag hindi tama yung tao na nailagay ninyo at nautosan,

6682
06:38:15,460 --> 06:38:17,900
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: magka-problema pa rin tayo sa pagkain.

6683
06:38:17,900 --> 06:38:18,540
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Thank you.

6684
06:38:18,680 --> 06:38:18,980
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

6685
06:38:19,660 --> 06:38:22,380
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, definitely, tama ko kayo.

6686
06:38:22,880 --> 06:38:30,840
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At nangyaring kami ng support pa sa inyo sa pagsulong ko ng agri-extension workers na kailangan na kailangan ng DA

6687
06:38:30,840 --> 06:38:35,800
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: para meron kayong sa bawat distrito, sa bawat munisipyo, meron talagang taga-DA,

6688
06:38:35,920 --> 06:38:39,600
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: diretso na nakatutok sa ating mga magsasakat mga isla.

6689
06:38:39,700 --> 06:38:40,440
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Thank you very much.

6690
06:38:41,480 --> 06:38:42,000
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Thank you, Chair.

6691
06:38:42,080 --> 06:38:42,940
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Thank you, Sekretary.

6692
06:38:43,160 --> 06:38:43,920
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Yes, sir.

6693
06:38:43,980 --> 06:38:44,360
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Mr. Chair.

6694
06:38:44,360 --> 06:38:45,120
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Thank you, Sekretary.

6695
06:38:45,120 --> 06:38:48,280
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: We promise po na bubutiin pa yung ating trabaho.

6696
06:38:48,680 --> 06:38:49,180
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Salamat po.

6697
06:38:49,300 --> 06:38:49,620
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Thank you, Pa.

6698
06:38:50,660 --> 06:38:55,880
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: The next interpellator from the Majority Leader, Christina Lopez.

6699
06:38:57,440 --> 06:38:58,900
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

6700
06:38:59,040 --> 06:39:00,160
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Good afternoon, everyone.

6701
06:39:00,380 --> 06:39:07,300
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Good afternoon, Sekretary Laurel of DA and kay Engineer Gullian ng NIA.

6702
06:39:07,960 --> 06:39:13,260
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: My question po is, Mr. Chair, para po sa DA,

6703
06:39:13,260 --> 06:39:16,180
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: from January to March 2026,

6704
06:39:16,180 --> 06:39:23,660
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: the average farmgate price of hogs for slaughter was quoted at P176 per kilogram.

6705
06:39:24,220 --> 06:39:33,860
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: This indicates a decrease of 16.1% from the previous year's same quarter quotation of P209 per kilogram,

6706
06:39:34,600 --> 06:39:37,420
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: according po to sa Philippine Statistics Authority.

6707
06:39:38,180 --> 06:39:46,080
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: By July 2026, an average retail price of P306 per kilogram at the national level was reported as P209 per kilogram.

6708
06:39:46,080 --> 06:39:46,160
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: At the national level was reported as P209 per kilogram at the national level was reported as P209 per kilogram.

6709
06:39:46,160 --> 06:39:47,420
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: This was noted for fresh pork.

6710
06:39:48,020 --> 06:39:50,140
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Fresh pork meat with bones.

6711
06:39:51,040 --> 06:39:55,640
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Kasi po, Mr. Chair, I'm from Quezon Province po.

6712
06:39:56,960 --> 06:40:00,160
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: And sa pag-ikot-ikot ko po sa mga barangay,

6713
06:40:00,640 --> 06:40:06,920
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: ang aming pong probinsya hindi lamang po mayaman sa dagat at sa mga gulay-gulay.

6714
06:40:07,540 --> 06:40:10,600
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Marami din po sa amin ang kabuhayan ay hayupan,

6715
06:40:10,940 --> 06:40:14,240
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: particularly po ang mga backyard hog raisers.

6716
06:40:14,680 --> 06:40:16,080
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Ngayon po, ang presyo na lamang,

6717
06:40:16,160 --> 06:40:21,380
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: po doon sa 150 pesos to 160.

6718
06:40:22,180 --> 06:40:23,060
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Napakababa po.

6719
06:40:23,840 --> 06:40:26,360
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Tumaas na po ang feeds at kung ano-ano na.

6720
06:40:26,760 --> 06:40:31,000
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Tapos ngayon po bumaba ang presyo ng live weight.

6721
06:40:31,500 --> 06:40:33,760
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: From DA po, mula po sa inyo,

6722
06:40:34,380 --> 06:40:36,360
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: ano po ba yung factors na naka-apekto?

6723
06:40:36,800 --> 06:40:39,500
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Sino po ang nagbibigay ng presyo sa livestock?

6724
06:40:40,060 --> 06:40:41,620
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: At ano na po bang nangyayari?

6725
06:40:41,620 --> 06:40:48,340
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Bakit patuloy na bumababa ang presyo ng live weight po natin ngayon?

6726
06:40:49,000 --> 06:40:51,820
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, tuloy-tuloy na pinag-aaralan ng DA,

6727
06:40:52,040 --> 06:40:53,880
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: especially yung ating livestock group,

6728
06:40:54,400 --> 06:40:55,920
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: ang situation na ito.

6729
06:40:56,040 --> 06:40:59,720
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Actually, sa Mindanao, meron pa tayong mga farmgate na 120 na lang.

6730
06:41:00,400 --> 06:41:01,600
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Or 130, no?

6731
06:41:02,260 --> 06:41:04,560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Ang phenomenon na nakikita namin,

6732
06:41:04,700 --> 06:41:07,200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: nangyari din ito last year but not as bad,

6733
06:41:07,320 --> 06:41:09,800
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: is basically yung ASF.

6734
06:41:10,680 --> 06:41:11,500
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Natatakot ngayon.

6735
06:41:11,500 --> 06:41:13,460
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Natatakot ng mga farmers na tamaan ng ASF,

6736
06:41:13,580 --> 06:41:14,800
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: lalo na sa rami ng ulan.

6737
06:41:15,280 --> 06:41:17,680
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Tuwing umuulan, lumalabas ulit ang ASF

6738
06:41:17,680 --> 06:41:19,260
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: dahil hindi hoon namamatay ang virus

6739
06:41:19,260 --> 06:41:21,400
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: kahit na binaon natin sa lupa ang baboy.

6740
06:41:22,020 --> 06:41:24,380
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So tuwing ulan, lumalabas ngayon sa groundwater

6741
06:41:24,380 --> 06:41:25,940
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: at bumabalik ang ASF.

6742
06:41:26,580 --> 06:41:29,560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At supply and demand ang nagdidikta ng presyo ngayon.

6743
06:41:29,700 --> 06:41:33,060
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Maraming hog farmers na nagpa-fast break

6744
06:41:33,060 --> 06:41:37,420
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: at ina-unload yung kanilang stocks

6745
06:41:38,520 --> 06:41:41,420
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: dahil nga natatakot na tamaan ng ASF.

6746
06:41:41,500 --> 06:41:45,000
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Dahil mayroon na sila sigurong narinig na may ASF na.

6747
06:41:45,800 --> 06:41:48,940
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Meron din akong kausap ng mga taga Mindanao

6748
06:41:48,940 --> 06:41:52,500
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: na biniblame nila yung importasyon ng baboy.

6749
06:41:53,600 --> 06:41:56,380
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pero pinakita ko sa kanila na sa Mindanao,

6750
06:41:56,760 --> 06:41:59,880
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: wala naman importasyon masyado ng baboy, no?

6751
06:42:00,380 --> 06:42:01,580
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa Pilipinas.

6752
06:42:02,240 --> 06:42:03,500
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: More of Luzon.

6753
06:42:03,840 --> 06:42:05,060
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pero ang presyo na 120.

6754
06:42:05,660 --> 06:42:11,080
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: That's what kaya ang assumption namin as of the moment

6755
06:42:11,080 --> 06:42:13,780
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: is nagpa-fast break din yung mga taga Mindanao

6756
06:42:13,780 --> 06:42:15,540
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: kasi nga natatakot sa ASF.

6757
06:42:16,080 --> 06:42:17,440
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Ang magandang balita naman,

6758
06:42:17,900 --> 06:42:21,760
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: siguro in coordination with kong Nicky Briones

6759
06:42:21,760 --> 06:42:23,520
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: at sa push din niya,

6760
06:42:24,080 --> 06:42:26,960
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: ay yung ating vaccine for ASF

6761
06:42:26,960 --> 06:42:31,520
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: ay ilalabas na natin this week ba, Yusek?

6762
06:42:31,900 --> 06:42:33,080
DA Undersecretary Constante J. Palabrica: Nailabas na, sir.

6763
06:42:33,340 --> 06:42:36,540
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Nailabas na yung ating for commercial use

6764
06:42:36,540 --> 06:42:37,780
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: ang ASF vaccine

6765
06:42:37,780 --> 06:42:40,920
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: at pwede nang bumili,

6766
06:42:41,080 --> 06:42:43,160
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: pag dumating yung stocks ng supplier,

6767
06:42:43,960 --> 06:42:47,380
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: ang ng ASF vaccine ng ating mga hog raisers

6768
06:42:47,380 --> 06:42:50,620
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: para maprotektahan nga at mag-stabilize ang presyo

6769
06:42:50,620 --> 06:42:54,220
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: ng baboy sa farm gate level, Mr. Chair.

6770
06:42:55,920 --> 06:42:57,260
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Thank you po, Osek.

6771
06:42:57,860 --> 06:42:59,540
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Ang follow-up question ko po dyan,

6772
06:42:59,960 --> 06:43:02,240
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: kung sinasabing nyo po ang Mindanao at Visayas,

6773
06:43:02,360 --> 06:43:05,840
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: okay po ang supply po nila ng karne po ngayon?

6774
06:43:08,160 --> 06:43:10,140
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: No, ang sinasabing ko lang, Mr. Chair,

6775
06:43:10,140 --> 06:43:12,380
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: is bagsak din ang presyo ng farm gate.

6776
06:43:12,420 --> 06:43:13,740
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa Visayas at Mindanao.

6777
06:43:14,300 --> 06:43:16,700
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Kung bagsak po ang farm gate,

6778
06:43:16,800 --> 06:43:19,980
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: ang presyo ng karne po sa buong Pilipinas,

6779
06:43:20,580 --> 06:43:25,540
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: gaano po kalaki ang ini-import po nating karne sa kasalukuyan?

6780
06:43:34,300 --> 06:43:38,940
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: I'm quite specific sa ating cuts

6781
06:43:38,940 --> 06:43:41,280
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: kasi ang main, Mr. Chair,

6782
06:43:41,360 --> 06:43:43,860
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: ang main na apektohan is yung pork cuts

6783
06:43:43,860 --> 06:43:44,740
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: tsaka bellies.

6784
06:43:44,740 --> 06:43:47,800
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yung pork cuts, yun yung kasim tsaka pigi.

6785
06:43:49,020 --> 06:43:51,480
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Sa data ng DA, actually,

6786
06:43:51,740 --> 06:43:54,600
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: 2025 was the highest in recent history, no?

6787
06:43:55,060 --> 06:43:59,480
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pero katulad ng pork bellies,

6788
06:44:00,540 --> 06:44:06,040
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: noong 2025, 9,000 tons a month ang importasyon.

6789
06:44:06,600 --> 06:44:10,480
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pero for 2026, bumaba siya to 8,000 tons a month lang.

6790
06:44:11,480 --> 06:44:15,560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pagdating sa pork cuts noong 2025,

6791
06:44:15,860 --> 06:44:18,560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: 29,800 tons.

6792
06:44:19,020 --> 06:44:21,720
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Tons a month siya.

6793
06:44:22,540 --> 06:44:28,320
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Pero 2026, as of August 24, 25,000 tons lang.

6794
06:44:28,400 --> 06:44:31,440
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So bumaba actually ang importasyon for this year

6795
06:44:31,440 --> 06:44:32,820
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: compared sa last year.

6796
06:44:33,420 --> 06:44:38,200
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: So it means healthy yung ating industry.

6797
06:44:38,740 --> 06:44:41,360
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Problema lang talaga, nagpa-fast break ang industriya

6798
06:44:41,360 --> 06:44:42,560
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: base sa datos ko.

6799
06:44:42,560 --> 06:44:43,740
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Thank you.

6800
06:44:44,400 --> 06:44:45,380
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Okay po.

6801
06:44:45,860 --> 06:44:47,120
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Kasi po, Sek,

6802
06:44:47,580 --> 06:44:48,680
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: bagsak po ang presyo.

6803
06:44:48,680 --> 06:44:50,900
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Sa Farmgate, pero ang presyo ng karne,

6804
06:44:51,780 --> 06:44:52,900
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: mataas pa rin po.

6805
06:44:54,000 --> 06:44:54,500
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Ano po?

6806
06:44:54,940 --> 06:44:58,000
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Ano po ba yung intervention na ginagawa po ng DA?

6807
06:44:58,460 --> 06:45:00,000
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Aside from importasyon.

6808
06:45:00,000 --> 06:45:07,800
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Tama po, okay lang po yan, may importation tayo. Pero short term, short term yung goal lang po ito.

6809
06:45:08,540 --> 06:45:14,860
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Ano po yung pang long term natin para po tayo makatulong sa ating mga farmers, sa ating hog raisers?

6810
06:45:15,560 --> 06:45:25,720
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Mr. Chair, I would just like to clarify na hindi, ang DA is not in favor of continuous importation.

6811
06:45:25,720 --> 06:45:32,740
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Ang position namin, kung pwedeng i-restrict yan, but unfortunately, meron tayong tinusunod na WTO rules.

6812
06:45:33,620 --> 06:45:35,720
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At pwede lang natin i-increase ay taripa.

6813
06:45:36,820 --> 06:45:43,720
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Nag-request na ho ang DA sa ating economic managers na kung pwedeng itaas ang taripa ng baboy at ibalik sa dating taripa.

6814
06:45:45,080 --> 06:45:52,160
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At ngayon, meron din tayong move na, and we are working with the tariff commission na yung jowls na tinatawag,

6815
06:45:52,160 --> 06:45:55,160
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: o kaya yung pangaba yun, ay i-classify.

6816
06:45:55,720 --> 06:46:03,920
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: I-classify na hindi na siya o-false, i-classify na siya at passport cut para itaas yung taripa.

6817
06:46:04,040 --> 06:46:10,760
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yun ho, yun lang ang madalis at pinakamabilis na supportang pwedeng ibigay natin sa ating mga hog raisers, Mr. Chair.

6818
06:46:15,730 --> 06:46:20,270
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Mr. Chair, I appreciate the explanation of Secretary Laurel.

6819
06:46:20,710 --> 06:46:25,530
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Siyempre po, ito po naman na inquiry lamang, pero siyempre po, at the end of the day,

6820
06:46:25,530 --> 06:46:30,050
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: this representation fully supports the approval of your budget.

6821
06:46:30,070 --> 06:46:38,930
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Sa bagong budget ng DA po at saka ng NIA, sana po huwag po natin kalimutan ang ating mga maliliit na backyard hog raisers.

6822
06:46:39,190 --> 06:46:41,410
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Yun lamang po, and thank you po, Mr. Chair.

6823
06:46:43,860 --> 06:46:52,660
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: Yes, definitely the DA would like to help the livestock sector, lalo na yung mga nagbababoy at nagmamanok.

6824
06:46:52,660 --> 06:47:00,660
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: At sa bagong budget na makukuha namin for the livestock, talagang repopulation and increase in population,

6825
06:47:01,740 --> 06:47:05,520
DA Secretary Francisco P. Tiu Laurel Jr.: langan para mabawasan ang importasyon at makalaban tayo, Mr. Chair.

6826
06:47:06,380 --> 06:47:13,880
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Thank you, Mr. Secretary. Thank you, Congresswoman Christina. The next

6827
06:47:13,960 --> 06:47:19,380
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Sa isa, from the minority, Representative Ma'am Zubiri.

6828
06:47:20,980 --> 06:47:27,120
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Maraming salamat po, Mr. Chair. At magandang hapon po sa ating mga bisita galing sa Department of Agriculture,

6829
06:47:27,780 --> 06:47:31,720
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: lalong-lalo na sa ating butihing Secretary, Secretary Francisco Chula.

6830
06:47:31,740 --> 06:47:33,420
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Magandang hapon po.

6831
06:47:34,180 --> 06:47:39,820
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Bago po ako mag-umpisa, sana payagan niyo po ako na magbida ng konti tungkol sa Bukidnon.

6832
06:47:40,440 --> 06:47:52,220
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Because this year po, naglabasan ng report for 2025 na Bukidnon is the top province in value of production in agriculture and fisheries and crop production

6833
06:47:52,220 --> 06:47:57,160
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: out of the 2.42 trillion pesos output of the Philippines.

6834
06:47:57,620 --> 06:48:01,700
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: And so out of that 2.42, ang Bukidnon po.

6835
06:48:01,740 --> 06:48:07,020
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Sa agriculture and fisheries, 162.3 billion pesos.

6836
06:48:07,460 --> 06:48:10,780
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Habang ang sumusunod po ay nasa 94.2 billion.

6837
06:48:11,240 --> 06:48:17,320
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Ang crop production po ng Bukidnon ay nasa 105.58 billion pesos.

6838
06:48:18,020 --> 06:48:21,020
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Habang ang sumusunod ay nasa 50.18 billion.

6839
06:48:21,580 --> 06:48:26,180
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Habang ang livestock po, out of the 420 billion ng country,

6840
06:48:26,640 --> 06:48:31,180
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: ang output coming from Bukidnon is 36.09 billion pesos.

6841
06:48:31,740 --> 06:48:35,920
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: And syempre, gusto ko po magpasalamat sa ating mga kaibigan sa DA.

6842
06:48:36,420 --> 06:48:43,920
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Dahil syempre, alam ko naman po na hindi natin ma-achieve ang mga numbers na ito kung wala ang full support ng Department of Agriculture

6843
06:48:43,920 --> 06:48:51,040
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: sa aming farms, sa aming mga farmers, and sa local government unit and provincial government unit ng Bukidnon.

6844
06:48:51,200 --> 06:48:54,460
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So thank you very much, Secretary, sa inyong full support.

6845
06:48:54,700 --> 06:48:58,480
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: And we hope na ngayong 2026, kami pa rin ang top performer.

6846
06:48:58,980 --> 06:49:00,580
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Now, having said this, no?

6847
06:49:01,740 --> 06:49:10,620
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: I would like to inquire, kasi given nga our numbers, may nabasa lang ako dito sa ating reports na medyo nalito lang ako ng konti.

6848
06:49:10,740 --> 06:49:20,560
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So I would like to ask for clarification from our friends sa NIA tungkol sa ating Bukidnon 3rd District budget from the NIA.

6849
06:49:21,520 --> 06:49:28,700
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Kasi ang nakalagay po dito was yung RDC endorsed noong 2025, nasa 772 million.

6850
06:49:28,700 --> 06:49:31,700
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Noong 2026, bumaba sa 500 million.

6851
06:49:31,740 --> 06:49:37,140
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Noong 2010, habang sa 2027, ang RDC endorsed is 273 million.

6852
06:49:37,820 --> 06:49:47,480
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: And may I clarify lang, kasi dito sa ating form dito, ang nakalagay sa NEP for Bukidnon 3rd District ay zero.

6853
06:49:48,040 --> 06:49:49,900
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: But I would like to clarify this, no?

6854
06:49:50,140 --> 06:49:57,420
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So we can discuss this further kung ano ba talaga ang tamang amount para sa Bukidnon with our friends from the NIA.

6855
06:49:57,420 --> 06:50:01,860
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Yes, Mr. Chair.

6856
06:50:02,220 --> 06:50:03,560
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Please just give me a time.

6857
06:50:04,100 --> 06:50:12,540
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Kasi siguro, gaya nga nang sabi ko, napakaganda ng mga output natin sa Bukidnon.

6858
06:50:12,760 --> 06:50:15,040
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So I would like to clarify this.

6859
06:50:21,630 --> 06:50:24,150
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Hindi naman siguro, kaya maganda mag-clarify muna.

6860
06:50:29,070 --> 06:50:35,850
Rep. Jose "Bong" J. Teves Jr.: Pinakamagandang record ang Bukidnon, tapos according to Congresswoman, is zero.

6861
06:50:43,030 --> 06:50:45,030
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Yes, ma'am actually

6862
06:50:45,510 --> 06:50:47,470
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Kaya ako nagulat din dahil na...

6863
06:50:49,110 --> 06:50:53,890
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Alam ko naman, ang Bukidnon talaga isa sa pinapangandang probinsya pagdating sa agrikultura.

6864
06:50:54,070 --> 06:50:55,910
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: So marami po kaming proposals.

6865
06:50:55,910 --> 06:51:03,590
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: And you know, pupunta kami sa opisina niyo, makikipag-tulungan po kami.

6866
06:51:03,950 --> 06:51:06,290
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Mag-courtesy na lang po kami.

6867
06:51:06,910 --> 06:51:07,270
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Ah, sige.

6868
06:51:07,450 --> 06:51:13,330
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So itong ating current figure dito, hindi pa naman final?

6869
06:51:14,970 --> 06:51:17,330
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Hindi lang nila na-update, Mr. Chair.

6870
06:51:17,490 --> 06:51:18,610
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Hindi lang nila na-update po.

6871
06:51:18,610 --> 06:51:21,530
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: I'm sorry, could you repeat that please?

6872
06:51:21,610 --> 06:51:22,370
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Hindi ko masyadong marinig.

6873
06:51:22,390 --> 06:51:25,490
NIA Administrator Eduardo Eddie G. Guillen: Yes, bukang hindi po nila, hindi po updated yung...

6874
06:51:25,490 --> 06:51:26,290
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Ah, okay. Hindi siya updated.

6875
06:51:26,850 --> 06:51:29,190
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Bukang, baka nahulog yung isang one.

6876
06:51:30,330 --> 06:51:31,870
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Sige, okay. I'm glad to hear that.

6877
06:51:31,950 --> 06:51:39,350
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Kasi syempre, you know, ayoko naman na hindi natin ma-keep up yung ating reputation as Bukidnon being the top producer.

6878
06:51:39,530 --> 06:51:44,990
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: E pag nawalan kami ng support from the NIA, may hirapan kami to produce all this agriculture,

6879
06:51:44,990 --> 06:51:47,830
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: which I think is very badly needed by our country.

6880
06:51:48,610 --> 06:51:54,290
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: And I would like to think that Department of Agriculture, especially NIA, will continue to support Bukidnon

6881
06:51:54,290 --> 06:51:57,330
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: para we can continue to support the country's agricultural needs.

6882
06:51:58,090 --> 06:52:00,430
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Okay, thank you very much to our director.

6883
06:52:01,130 --> 06:52:05,050
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Our second doc, my second question, of course, goes to our friends from the SRA.

6884
06:52:06,330 --> 06:52:07,670
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Hi, good afternoon, Admin.

6885
06:52:08,410 --> 06:52:10,510
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Kamusta na, Admin Ascona?

6886
06:52:11,170 --> 06:52:14,350
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Good afternoon po, Mr. Chair. Good afternoon, ma'am.

6887
06:52:14,350 --> 06:52:15,290
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: May hapon.

6888
06:52:15,410 --> 06:52:18,590
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So, last year, I remember we worked quite closely.

6889
06:52:18,610 --> 06:52:23,470
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: And trying to increase the budget, or actually trying to increase the budget of the SRA.

6890
06:52:23,690 --> 06:52:30,390
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Because, syempre, as a sugar-producing province, talagang nakikita namin ang impact at ang napakalaking effect at tulong ng SRA.

6891
06:52:30,770 --> 06:52:35,050
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: And we wanted to increase your budget from 2 billion to maybe 3 or 4, no?

6892
06:52:35,510 --> 06:52:41,370
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Kaya lang, I was very disappointed to find out that, number one, hindi natin na-increase ang inyong budget.

6893
06:52:41,930 --> 06:52:47,490
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: And even more so, more disappointed to discover na yung 2 billion na dapat naka-alot sa inyo,

6894
06:52:47,730 --> 06:52:48,590
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: 1 billion na naka-alot sa inyo.

6895
06:52:48,610 --> 06:52:51,370
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So, 1 billion pa rin lang ang naibigay sa inyo sa ating last budget.

6896
06:52:52,210 --> 06:52:58,510
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Do you mind updating me on why, what was the final explanation? Bakit 1 billion lang napunta sa inyo?

6897
06:52:59,610 --> 06:53:05,370
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Yeah, Mr. Chair, we were informed of, once again, utilization problems.

6898
06:53:06,170 --> 06:53:13,370
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: So, there has been new guidelines on procurement, which actually delayed a lot of our utilization.

6899
06:53:13,930 --> 06:53:18,370
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: So, we're still hoping to make it up in the last 3 years.

6900
06:53:18,610 --> 06:53:29,070
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: We're also planning po, ma'am, to reallocate some of the budget into our quick response fund for the RSSI infection,

6901
06:53:29,690 --> 06:53:34,150
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: as well as the mitigation on El Niño.

6902
06:53:35,610 --> 06:53:40,490
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: What programs or mandates of the SRA are currently affected by this lack of budget?

6903
06:53:40,750 --> 06:53:42,050
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Would you be able to tell me?

6904
06:53:43,830 --> 06:53:45,790
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Or because of the insufficient appropriations?

6905
06:53:45,790 --> 06:53:47,510
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Yeah, well, Mr. Chair,

6906
06:53:48,610 --> 06:53:52,330
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: since the SIDA program po is pre-allocated by the law,

6907
06:53:52,890 --> 06:53:57,430
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: so, from 2 billion to 1 billion po, it cuts everything by 50%.

6908
06:53:57,430 --> 06:54:00,550
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: So, malaki po yung effect sa amin po.

6909
06:54:01,190 --> 06:54:05,010
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So, parang across the board, talagang naka-annuation proportion din siya?

6910
06:54:05,430 --> 06:54:12,010
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So, lahat yan, kasama yung ating mga infrastructure, yung ating mga block farm programs, ating mga scholarships, no?

6911
06:54:12,490 --> 06:54:17,270
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Lahat yan matatamaan, especially, and I think this is not the time for that to happen,

6912
06:54:17,270 --> 06:54:18,270
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: given na ang lakas.

6913
06:54:18,610 --> 06:54:24,770
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Okay, ng threat ng El Niño na hinaharap natin, and syempre yung ating RSSI.

6914
06:54:25,470 --> 06:54:29,370
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: And with regard to RSSI, I'm very happy because the last time nag-usap tayo,

6915
06:54:29,370 --> 06:54:36,830
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: alam ko na nga ako ang SRA na maghahatid kayo ng Presidential Assistance for Farmers program sa Bukidnon.

6916
06:54:37,270 --> 06:54:39,570
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: May I ask on the status of that current program?

6917
06:54:40,290 --> 06:54:42,490
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Yeah, we're still ongoing po, ma'am, on the releases.

6918
06:54:43,210 --> 06:54:48,490
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Yung total po na ayuda for the whole industry, umabot na ng 420-something.

6919
06:54:48,610 --> 06:54:49,110
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: Million.

6920
06:54:49,970 --> 06:54:58,890
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: So, we have, this is, most of it is coming from the SWD, and as of my last knowledge,

6921
06:54:59,050 --> 06:55:02,050
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: we released, I think, almost 100 million already.

6922
06:55:02,530 --> 06:55:04,450
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: So, this is farmers and workers na po.

6923
06:55:04,750 --> 06:55:07,970
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Out of that 100 billion, how much was allocated for Bukidnon?

6924
06:55:08,990 --> 06:55:11,610
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: I am not currently aware of the percentage, ma'am.

6925
06:55:11,690 --> 06:55:13,290
SRA Administrator Pablo Luis S. Azcona: I'll provide you with the information.

6926
06:55:13,670 --> 06:55:15,870
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Okay, I will look forward to that information.

6927
06:55:15,870 --> 06:55:18,450
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Sana, since given that Bukidnon is one of the...

6928
06:55:18,450 --> 06:55:21,510
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: one of the biggest sugar-producing portions of our country,

6929
06:55:21,930 --> 06:55:26,230
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: and currently, actually, nag-umpisa tayo at only about 30 hectares.

6930
06:55:26,730 --> 06:55:34,490
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Pero sa ngayon, ang aking latest calculation na natanggap ay nasa 576 hectares na in just a span of 3 months.

6931
06:55:34,670 --> 06:55:38,590
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So, I'm deeply concerned as to how much more we're going to be looking at.

6932
06:55:39,170 --> 06:55:44,290
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: And my last question is, of course, for our friends from the DA and Region 10,

6933
06:55:44,290 --> 06:55:48,270
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: ang understanding ko is, meron kayong request, no?

6934
06:55:48,450 --> 06:55:57,050
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: For expanding our laboratory budget, for our laboratory budget from our DA in Region 10.

6935
06:55:58,250 --> 06:56:03,990
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Currently, magkano ba ang budget na nakatanggap ng ating regional office

6936
06:56:03,990 --> 06:56:09,590
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: para sa mga biological control and other issues such as that?

6937
06:56:09,830 --> 06:56:13,880
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Hello po.

6938
06:56:15,100 --> 06:56:18,960
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Yung, in terms of capacity to respond to RISIS-I,

6939
06:56:19,700 --> 06:56:21,500
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: early first quarter, yun.

6940
06:56:21,520 --> 06:56:22,720
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: We have 5 hectares per day.

6941
06:56:22,980 --> 06:56:27,680
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Now, when the RISIS-I reaches up to 1.1% infection rate,

6942
06:56:27,800 --> 06:56:30,240
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: we raise our capacity to 20 hectares.

6943
06:56:30,740 --> 06:56:35,740
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Three weeks ago, we have a discussion with the SRA in Bukidnon.

6944
06:56:36,020 --> 06:56:39,580
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: We raise it to 30 hectares, which means every day,

6945
06:56:40,120 --> 06:56:43,440
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: we can supply biological control up to 30 hectares per day,

6946
06:56:43,440 --> 06:56:51,240
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: totaling to, in a week, we can actually supply up to 3, 6, 9, 12, 15,

6947
06:56:51,520 --> 06:56:53,620
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: 150 hectares.

6948
06:56:54,340 --> 06:56:57,100
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: We computed it in terms of the infection rate.

6949
06:56:57,960 --> 06:56:59,780
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: I don't have the specific budget,

6950
06:56:59,780 --> 06:57:04,340
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: but I want to respond on our capacity to deliver response to RISIS-I.

6951
06:57:04,840 --> 06:57:06,000
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Before the end of this year,

6952
06:57:06,240 --> 06:57:09,200
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: our estimate is that we can respond up to 100 hectares per day,

6953
06:57:09,460 --> 06:57:15,060
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: which is more than enough with the infection rate of around 0.7% per month since January.

6954
06:57:15,860 --> 06:57:20,940
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: So, we have also a plan to increase first quarter of next year.

6955
06:57:21,520 --> 06:57:27,220
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: So, that we can apply every day 100 hectares,

6956
06:57:27,620 --> 06:57:38,380
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: so that it is more than enough with the existing 2.2% infected sugarcane out of 45,000 hectares.

6957
06:57:38,380 --> 06:57:47,880
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: So, yung estimate namin, if we work together with SRA in responding farmers who want biological control,

6958
06:57:48,360 --> 06:57:49,640
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: in the next three months,

6959
06:57:50,200 --> 06:57:51,280
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: kaya namin i-maintain,

6960
06:57:51,520 --> 06:57:55,180
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: 2.5% o yung makarecover po.

6961
06:57:55,180 --> 06:58:02,760
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Ang tinitinan lang namin, yung early infestation at saka yung nasa low pa,

6962
06:58:03,000 --> 06:58:04,020
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: yun yung i-respond namin.

6963
06:58:04,400 --> 06:58:06,060
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Ngayon, we have mapped out yung direction.

6964
06:58:06,260 --> 06:58:07,780
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Saan ba pumupunta yung RISIS-I?

6965
06:58:08,040 --> 06:58:09,500
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: From east to west, from west to ano.

6966
06:58:09,880 --> 06:58:13,600
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: So that, more or less, we can preposition our inputs.

6967
06:58:13,740 --> 06:58:16,020
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Right now, we have 150 million,

6968
06:58:16,380 --> 06:58:20,320
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: more or less, 150 million that we propose as a quick response fund

6969
06:58:20,320 --> 06:58:21,380
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: to increase our...

6970
06:58:21,520 --> 06:58:22,840
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: capacity sa laboratory

6971
06:58:22,840 --> 06:58:28,000
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: so that we will not reach up to 5% infection rate.

6972
06:58:28,300 --> 06:58:31,720
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Right now, the DE has identified three levels of infection.

6973
06:58:31,720 --> 06:58:38,820
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: The below, low, moderate, at saka severe.

6974
06:58:39,360 --> 06:58:42,220
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: So, according with that classification,

6975
06:58:42,880 --> 06:58:47,080
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: we can exactly respond to the situation

6976
06:58:47,080 --> 06:58:49,080
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: knowing that before the end of this year,

6977
06:58:49,140 --> 06:58:50,500
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: we can increase our capacity po.

6978
06:58:51,520 --> 06:58:52,860
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Ang gays.

6979
06:58:56,870 --> 06:58:57,170
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Okay.

6980
06:58:57,370 --> 06:58:59,470
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So, I'm glad to hear na meron tayong mga plano.

6981
06:58:59,630 --> 06:59:02,750
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Pero ang tanong ko is, kahit ma-increase natin yung capacity natin,

6982
06:59:02,810 --> 06:59:04,450
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: eventually before the end of the year,

6983
06:59:04,510 --> 06:59:06,430
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: as you said, to how many hectares per day,

6984
06:59:06,810 --> 06:59:09,950
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: mahahabol ba natin yung ating infection rate?

6985
06:59:10,050 --> 06:59:12,110
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Kasi right now, nakita natin from 30 hectares,

6986
06:59:12,230 --> 06:59:15,390
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: nasa 576 na tayo in just three months.

6987
06:59:15,530 --> 06:59:17,710
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So, in another one to two months,

6988
06:59:17,830 --> 06:59:22,270
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: baka yung 576 nasa 1,000 plus hectares na or even 2,000.

6989
06:59:22,270 --> 06:59:23,750
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So, mahahabol ba?

6990
06:59:23,990 --> 06:59:24,750
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Kahit ma-increase?

6991
06:59:24,830 --> 06:59:25,690
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Itong ating capacity?

6992
06:59:26,030 --> 06:59:26,550
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Yes po.

6993
06:59:26,670 --> 06:59:32,110
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Kasi kasama nung ginawa yung Crystal Milling Corporation,

6994
06:59:32,510 --> 06:59:34,730
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: we helped them start their own laboratory.

6995
06:59:35,190 --> 06:59:36,070
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Kahit yung sa Busco.

6996
06:59:36,310 --> 06:59:39,390
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: In fact, our meeting last time with Mr. Lorenzo,

6997
06:59:39,490 --> 06:59:42,190
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: who heads the farmers group for sugarcane,

6998
06:59:42,270 --> 06:59:44,170
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: he only needs 20 hectares per day.

6999
06:59:44,250 --> 06:59:44,910
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: That was July.

7000
06:59:45,450 --> 06:59:47,310
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: But we were able to increase it up to 30.

7001
06:59:47,690 --> 06:59:51,370
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: So, with the participation of private sector who owns laboratory,

7002
06:59:52,310 --> 06:59:54,470
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: we can actually maintain it, ma'am,

7003
06:59:55,170 --> 06:59:56,270
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: not beyond 5 percent.

7004
06:59:56,410 --> 06:59:59,990
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Right now, with the increasing participation of owners of...

7005
07:00:00,000 --> 07:00:09,400
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: milling company na dalawa sa bukid nun. Sa tingin ko before the end of this year, kaya namin nating hindi lalag pa sa 5% po.

7006
07:00:09,720 --> 07:00:12,680
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: That's good to hear. That's good news. Thank you very much, Director Pacamalan.

7007
07:00:13,220 --> 07:00:21,080
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: And so as a final question, magkano kaya ang kailangan na budget ng DA Region 10 in order to reach that capacity,

7008
07:00:21,220 --> 07:00:23,520
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: to increase para maabot niyo yung capacity na yan?

7009
07:00:23,520 --> 07:00:30,920
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Yung disubmit namin as part ng Quick Response Fund is nasa P150 million po.

7010
07:00:31,060 --> 07:00:31,620
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: Magkano po?

7011
07:00:31,900 --> 07:00:32,840
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: P150 million.

7012
07:00:32,860 --> 07:00:42,560
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: P150 million, yes. And sa tingin natin itong magkano ang mawawala sa atin kung ang bukid nun,

7013
07:00:42,680 --> 07:00:47,920
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: hindi natin makontrol ang RSSI at grumabit talaga ito, mawalan talaga ng kontrol, magkano mawawala sa atin?

7014
07:00:47,920 --> 07:00:53,460
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: Malaki po kasi bukid nun has 45,000 hectares of sugarcane and I think that's more than a billion.

7015
07:00:53,520 --> 07:01:01,960
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: And the reason why we automatically increase our capacity is we are very conscious about not going beyond 5%.

7016
07:01:01,960 --> 07:01:05,100
DA Region X Regional Executive Director Jose Apollo Y. Pacamalan: It's very important commodity in bukid nun talaga.

7017
07:01:05,440 --> 07:01:11,420
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: So parang bali yung ating increase is not even 10% of how much value we are getting from bukid nun, no?

7018
07:01:11,800 --> 07:01:17,520
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: And given the fact na bukid nun is producing not just sugar but also corn and palay, which can also be affected by RSSI,

7019
07:01:17,520 --> 07:01:22,720
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: I think this is a very small investment with very large returns for the DA.

7020
07:01:23,520 --> 07:01:25,420
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: We can get that funded po, Secretary.

7021
07:01:26,200 --> 07:01:32,840
Rep. Audrey Kay T. Zubiri: And of course, Mr. Secretary, I would also like to add na yun nga yung ating sa SRA,

7022
